                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[h1] An interesting game that will get your brain moving [/h1]\nMachineers is a very cool idea for an adventure, or rather a series of mini-games sprinkled with a point and click story.\nWe play as a robot woman who is thrown into the middle of the robot world, - to get further she has to help everyone in turn, of her own free will or not. \n Everyone we meet will want and need something, and we have to set the algorithm for the movement of the bird's wings so that both wings flap at the same time, and someone else will ask us to reorganize the machine so that all the LEDs on the signboard light up at once - the concept is the same, but in different forms.\nThe games are based mainly on the same concept, i.e. arranging the gears and chains in such a way as the game requires.\nThe graphics are interesting, paper cut-outs in a steampunk atmosphere. \nIn my opinion, a very pleasant item, and worth buying especially on promotion for little money.",
